                           <td>The patient’s estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) is mildly decreased (62 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with stage 2-3a chronic kidney disease, which is not uncommon at this age. Renal function should be monitored periodically, and potential risk factors or nephrotoxic medications should be reviewed. No acute abnormality detected.</td>
